    "result_text": "All green \u2014 build succeeds and the acceptance test passes. The audit line confirms the new format: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (NSW + FY `27` for a 2026\u201109\u201107 registration + HASH8 `16E6609E` + Luhn CHK `1`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nUnified the identity into a single `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, keeping the entity's internal `customer_code` column as opaque storage (so the large `Owner` class and the DB schemas stay untouched \u2014 the removed fields are the exposed DTO ones).\n\n- **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now composes `region + 2-digit FY + HASH8 + Luhn CHK` and stores it. Reuses the existing `hash8`, `FiscalYear.of`, and `CheckDigit`.\n- **`CheckDigit.java`** \u2014 generalized `of(Owner)` \u2192 `of(String)`, a pure Luhn-over-a-string helper now used for the CHK segment (and no longer coupled to `customerCode`).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipNumber` mapping with `memberId` (the stored value), dropped the `checkDigit` mapping, and repointed `locality`/`timezone` from parsing the old `<REGION>-...` string to `Locality.of(city, postcode)` directly (the new id has no separator to split on).\n- **`LogAuditOnCreate.java`** \u2014 the audit line and the structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` now carry `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema fields; added `memberId`.\n\nCollision handling needed no change: `DeduplicateCustomerCode` already dedups the stored value, which is now the memberId. `OwnerSegment` and the `fiscalYear` field already derive from locality/registration date and stay consistent with the memberId's REGION/FY segments.\n\nI kept the surrounding class name and pipeline wiring intact so the YAML and the rest of the endpoint didn't move.",
